# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staged-build worktree (scripts/build_staged.py): each build compiles a
# snapshot of HEAD there, so Quartus scratch stays out of the repo root and
# the main tree stays editable during the compile. See docs/WORKFLOW.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
quartus_*.log
q_*.log
sta*.log
worst_*.rpt
compile.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ModelSim
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
work/
# every ModelSim library this project's runners create: work/ (run_sim.sh),
# work_nofp/ (run_v60_tests.sh's no-FP profile), work_bus/ (ad-hoc)
work_*/
transcript
vsim.wlf
modelsim.ini
*.vstf
sim/**/*.log
sim/**/*.bin
sim/**/*.lst
sim/**/*.hex
sim/**/*.raw
sim/**/*.trace
sim/**/*.dec
sim/**/*dump*.txt
sim/**/fixture.txt
# Vendored cores' SIMULATION-only dumps, written into whatever CWD the
# simulator runs from.
/*.raw

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copyrighted MAME ROM dumps -- used locally for bring-up and for building
# the ROM images the .mra files describe. NEVER committed, in any
# subdirectory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
roms/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local hardware-debug scratch: screenshots pulled back off the MiSTer,
# decoded probe captures, ad-hoc analysis output.
#
# Root-only. Anchored with a leading slash because a bare `debug/` matches
# ANY directory of that name at any depth, which on the Fuuki core silently
# swallowed rtl/debug/ -- the core's own instrumentation source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/debug/
/*.png
/*.txt
scratch_*.png
scratch_*.txt
cfg.bin
outfile.bin

# MAME's own state directories, written into whatever directory MAME was
# launched from.
cfg/
nvram/
snap/
sta/

# Local MiSTer connection settings (host/user/password) for the deploy
# scripts -- never committed.
mister.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# releases/ IS the right home for built bitstreams, but only a build VERIFIED
# to actually run the games belongs in git. Committing one that merely
# compiles is actively misleading. Add a good one deliberately:
#   git add -f "releases/<name>.rbf"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
releases/*.rbf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# SignalTap file Quartus drops beside a project it opens
*.sld
